=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, ${{b}_{1},2{b}_{2}}$ spans ${R}^{2}$ since any linear combination of $B$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${{b}_{1},2{b}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}={x}_{1}{b}_{1}+\\frac{{x}_{2}}{2}(2{b}_{2})\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The set ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2},2{c}_{2}}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the third vector is a linear combination of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ This means that the set is linearly dependent and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139535529 true] [17592186353770 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353771 13194139535529 true] [17592186353770 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353772 13194139535529 true] [17592186353770 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353773 13194139535529 true] [17592186353770 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353774 13194139535529 true] [17592186353770 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353775 13194139535529 true] [17592186353770 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535529 true] [17592186353770 1041 "selection" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353770 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353775 13194139535529 true] [17592186353770 1110 #uuid "1758a1b1-69cf-577d-92ca-1ab266980a8e" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353771 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353771 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535529 true] [17592186353771 1111 #uuid "bb453a8e-014a-5cd2-abd8-6272f1dc3238" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353772 1034 "I only" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353772 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535529 true] [17592186353772 1111 #uuid "49f28852-232d-5754-9e8f-2366ec800378" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353773 1034 "III only" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353773 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535529 true] [17592186353773 1111 #uuid "2e4cf03d-8eeb-510c-9e97-0d2e349d40bf" 13194139535529 true]