alse. The set ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the set contains vectors from another vector space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true\"." 13194139535529 true] [17592186353777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353778 13194139535529 true] [17592186353777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353779 13194139535529 true] [17592186353777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353780 13194139535529 true] [17592186353777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353781 13194139535529 true] [17592186353777 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353782 13194139535529 true] [17592186353777 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535529 true] [17592186353777 1041 "selection" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353777 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353778 13194139535529 true] [17592186353777 1110 #uuid "b888e468-d320-5adc-a2a7-c054ea88d2a2" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353778 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353778 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535529 true] [17592186353778 1111 #uuid "834fa4d7-0c05-5971-a9a7-54c93fc76925" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353779 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535529 true] [17592186353779 1111 #uuid "f2d4a048-5675-5dfa-9661-5fe06cd1a3be" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353780 1034 "III only" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353780 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535529 true] [17592186353780 1111 #uuid "9df18407-fec2-5aa4-8d94-d0e308995148" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353781 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535529 true] [17592186353781 1111 #uuid "4c3cd5ea-1b33-57df-95fb-ba287b358e49" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353782 1034 "II only" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535529 true] [17592186353782 1111 #uuid "5796c6ba-49b7-51a0-8c3c-40ca6c808c84" 13194139535529 true] [17592186353783 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353784 13194139535529 true] [17592186353783 1089 "q-34768" 13194139535